  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-22T22:16:37.488Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "TLDR: Change the avatar performance ranks from good/poor to very high optimized , high optimized, optimized, low optimized, very low optimized.\n\n\nThe new avatar performance tab has been a much requested suggestion but it has also drawn a lot of unhappy opinions.\n\nWhile there are a few reasons why one of which I believe is simply due to word choice.\n\nWord choice is very important as we have found out with other features like the rankings even if the process is the same just how it is worded can make a lot of difference.\n\nIn vrchat your avatar is your representation of yourself.  Some people put avatars on like clothes changing them regularly others have personal avatars that is them and only them in vrchat.  How these personal avatars are referenced can cause issues.\n\nThe avatar performance ranks of good and poor are not the best words to use as these are not technical words but more personal descriptors.  When you have your own personal avatar and check its performance and see its poor or very poor it can get peoples backs up.  They get defensive.\n\nIts simply a technical process your telling them there avatar is not optimized and how it is not but by calling there avatar poor or very poor they feel your downing there avatar.\n\nI suggest simply change the reference to optimized instead of having: very good, good, poor and very poor instead have very high optimized , high optimized, optimized, low optimized, very low optimized.\n\nThis means your describing there avatar in a technical way rather than a personal way.\n\nLastly it also gives new players who are starting to make avatars a reason why your calling there avatar poor or even good.  They know its because there optimization.",
